       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is above the usual maximum for ibuprofen. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, and the labeled maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day. Even with normal kidney and liver function, that dose carries a meaningful risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **1,600 mg PO every 6 hours as needed**, or 1,600 mg PO three times daily, or 1,200 mg PO four times daily (or similar, depending on the clinical goal)\n\nPlease have the treating physician or a prescriber confirm the intended dose and frequency. Once they do, I can enter it. Since you're not a clinician, the prescriber should also be the one to submit the order, or at least confirm it directly."
      }
