       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. A confirmation from you doesn't change the dose-safety issue, and you're not a prescriber, so I can't treat your confirmation as clinical sign-off.\n\nIbuprofen 1,600 mg four times daily (6,400 mg/day) is twice the labeled adult maximum of 3,200 mg/day. Please have the treating physician or another licensed prescriber review it. They can either:\n\n- Submit a corrected dose, such as 800 mg PO four times daily, and I'll enter it.\n- Document a clinical reason for a dose above the labeled maximum, and submit the order themselves through the proper ordering system.\n\nIf the prescriber asks me to enter the order with a specific dose and frequency, I can do that, with a note recording their name and rationale."
      }
